From 4ef908f9e6b70c0422615179e0e8f395cff92a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Rehn <andreas.rehn@mercedes-benz.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 03:31:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] port: replace ION+chardev with DRM/accel+GEM interface

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded platform specific]

Replace the ION allocator and /dev/cvi-tpu0 chardev interface with
DRM/accel subsystem using GEM buffer objects via /dev/accel/accel0.

Key changes:
- bm_npu_ioctl.h: Replace vendor ioctls with DRM_IOCTL_SOPHGO_TPU_*
  wrappers using <drm/drm.h> and <sophgo/sophgo_tpu.h>
- mem_alloc: ION alloc -> DRM_IOCTL_SOPHGO_TPU_CREATE_BO + mmap
- mem_free: close(dma_fd) -> DRM_IOCTL_GEM_CLOSE via thread_local fd
- submit_dmabuf: Now takes GEM handle + cmdbuf_size instead of dma_fd
- wait_dmabuf: Uses DRM_IOCTL_SOPHGO_TPU_WAIT with seq_no + timeout
- mem_flush_ext/mem_invld_ext: Uses DRM_IOCTL_SOPHGO_TPU_SYNC
- Remove ion_fd/ion_heap_id from bm_device_t
- Remove ion_ioctl() and ion_query_heap() entirely
- TEE functions stubbed out (not supported in DRM path)

Signed-off-by: Andreas Rehn <rehn.andreas86@gmail.com>
